# This .gitignore ships as part of the template and becomes your project's .gitignore.
#
# NOTE: BMAD's install (the _bmad/ framework + .claude/skills/bmad-*) is intentionally NOT ignored. It is
# installed at project init by scripts/setup.sh (`npx bmad-method install`) and COMMITTED to your project —
# the same as the source project this template derives from — so the SDLC tooling lives in the repo at a
# pinned version. BMAD's own nested _bmad/custom/.gitignore keeps personal config (_bmad/custom/*.user.toml)
# out of git; nothing else BMAD generates is ignored.

# Backlog.md transient locks (task state itself IS committed under backlog/)
backlog/.locks/

# Local orchestration / agent state (not part of the project)
.omc/
.remember/

# ── Your language toolchain ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This template is stack-agnostic. Add your project's dependency + build output here once you pick a stack:
#   node_modules/  dist/  *.tsbuildinfo          (Node / TypeScript)
#   __pycache__/   .venv/  *.pyc  .pytest_cache/ (Python)
#   target/        Cargo.lock~                   (Rust)
#   bin/  vendor/                                (Go)

# ── OS / editor cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
*.swp
